   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the New York city health and hospitals corporation act, in\nrelation to requiring compliance with the city's uniform land use review\nprocedure for the disposition of land or buildings by the corporation",
    "basePrintNo": "S6685",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6685-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §5, NYC Health & Hosp Corp Act",
    "lawSection": "New York City Health and Hospitals Corporation Act",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S6685\n\nSPONSOR: CLEARE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the New York city health and hospitals corporation act,\nin relation to requiring compliance with the city's uniform land use\nreview procedure for the disposition of land or buildings by the corpo-\nration\n\n \nPURPOSE:  To require NYC HHC to adhere to the Uniform Land Use Review\nProcedure (ULURP).\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nAmends various sections of the NYC HHC Law to provide that when the\nCorporation seeks to dispose of land or buildings, they comply with\nULURP.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nMuch has changed since the New York city health and hospitals corpo-\nration act was enacted in 1969. For example, the modern day ULURP Proc-\ness would not be formalized until 1975. No credible reading of the HHC\nStatute could conclude that ULURP should not be the baseline standard\nwhich the Corporation should follow in the rare instances where they\nseek to dispose of land or buildings, particularly for non-medical uses.\nThe Community must have a formal voice-it is that simple.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nUndetermined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n180 Days.\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
